# 8. Campaign Pacing and Player Experience

The campaign should alternate intentionally between:

- Exploration.
- Narrative discovery.
- Environmental interaction.
- Combat.
- Quiet moments.
- Boss encounters.
- Progression.
- Revelation.

Avoid placing multiple long dialogue sequences back-to-back.

Avoid making every area a combat encounter.

Allow the player moments to observe the world and understand what happened there.

Use the existing:
- Weapon progression.
- Upgrade Bench.
- Enemy tactical archetypes.
- Encounter compositions.
- Traversal routes.
- Timed hazards.
- Secret areas.
- Sector Map.
- Mission journal.
- Codex.

Connect existing systems to the story rather than adding unrelated systems.

Optional exploration should feel worthwhile without making campaign completion dependent on collecting everything.

The player should be able to complete the primary narrative without discovering every secret.

However, players who explore deeply should gain additional context and a richer understanding of the world.

